    {
      "line_no": 7,
      "code": "    CHECK",
      "explanation": "This example is to specify the total number of sailors and boats should be less 100. However, this example is WRONG. This check constraint which checks both 'sailor' and 'boats' tables belongs to 'sailors' table itself recursively. If sailors is empty, the number of Boats tuples can be anything!"
    },
    {
      "line_no": 8,
      "code": "    ((SELECT COUNT(S.sid) ",
      "explanation": "<b>This first example is WRONG.</b> If sailors is empty, the number of Boats tuples can be anything! It returns the number sailor id. The most nested query is executed firstly. "
    },
    {
      "line_no": 9,
      "code": "     FROM sailor S) + ",
      "explanation": "Two separate queries are linked using summation sign. Both query results are sum up. "
    },
    {
      "line_no": 10,
      "code": "    (SELECT COUNT(B.sid) ",
      "explanation": "This query returns the number of boats."
    },
